## Lab vs Natural Marquise Diamond Earrings

[![Bezel marquise diamond stud earrings 1 CTW 14k yellow gold studio shot](/images/marquise-diamond-stud-earrings-yellow-gold.jpg)](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/earrings/bezel-diamond-stud-earrings-with-1-ctw-marquise-cut-diamonds-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-297407?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=Image)

Lab-grown marquise diamonds are physically and chemically identical to natural. The [GIA](https://www.gia.edu/) grades them on the same 4Cs scale. The [IGI](https://www.igi.org/) provides the same certification standards. The origin is different — lab-grown rather than earth-mined. The diamond is not.

Every product in this guide has a lab-grown option accessible via the product page. Lab versions at equivalent CTW typically save 40–70% compared to natural.

At 1 CTW natural bezel studs: [$5,200 in white gold](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/earrings/bezel-diamond-stud-earrings-with-1-ctw-marquise-cut-diamonds-in-14k-white-gold-item-297401?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). The lab version at the same CTW comes in substantially under that on the same product page — and that savings lets you jump to 1.5 CTW or 2 CTW at or below the natural 1 CTW price.

This is the most impactful use of the lab savings in earrings: rather than buying the same CTW for less money, buy a higher CTW for the same money. The visual jump from 1 CTW to 2 CTW on the ear is significant. The stones look meaningfully larger. Your overall jewelry presence is stronger.

